    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 14 tests, 0 failures. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. Changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it appears on both the request body and the `Owner` response DTO (generated as a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`, `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the create pipeline's build step now defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the mapped value is null; a supplied date passes through unchanged. (MapStruct maps the field by name in both directions.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the owners table in all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql).\n\nBoth new tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
